  "_weights_note": "weight = relative share of treatment episodes before repeat claims (dialysis/chemo add extra rows). Illustrative.",
  "_repeat_note": "Dialysis and chemotherapy repeat patterns were calibrated against a 1,164-patient Synthea run (dialysis: median gap 3.1 days, median ~258 sessions/patient over its history; breast-cancer chemotherapy: median gap ~22 days, median 8 cycles). Synthea is US-based, so this is consistency with a clinical simulator, not Indian ground truth.",
  "_rates_note": "HBP 2.2 sets medical packages per bed-day (routine ward 2100, HDU 3300, ICU without ventilator 8500, ICU with ventilator 9000). No normal-delivery package exists in the HBP master, so PKG-08 is high risk delivery. Coronary angiography alone is not a package (PTCA includes it), so PKG-03 is heart catheterization. Where a package has several procedures or implants, one representative procedure is used.",
